<p>Iran launched waves of missile and drone strikes across the Gulf overnight into March 1, damaging Dubai International Airport and the Burj Al Arab hotel. Explosions were also reported around Palm Jumeirah, where residents and visitors evacuated affected areas. Debris from an intercepted drone sparked a fire at the base of the Burj Al Arab. Multiple outlets described the attacks as Iranian retaliation for U.S. and Israeli strikes on Iranian targets on February 28. The escalation appeared to extend beyond U.S. military sites to civilian areas and major transport hubs. Across the region, Bahrain reported strikes in Manama, including on a security-related building and near a U.S. base. Kuwait reported Shahed drones hitting its international airport. Several Gulf states said they intercepted incoming missiles, and Qatar said it had foiled attacks. Officials and news reports emphasized interceptions, rapid-response measures, and civil-defense guidance as authorities worked to contain damage and restore normal operations where possible.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/iUmTzXqO6w7BrMUkUQQDHXkIBz_i04WgEPVJdWOBbx168moGsV8MaxWil3p29fuqJcxkLEAPqR4NWjfV1wTyrlm-K3sytHe7J8h0CWpPbwkcddavlQ3d4iB4GfnSg9rv1rDuHLUZcNajSmBa0PtlA0DxcqLZzkWuXZ2qmNgWMwydJ34d9JM0fBUS-La_0TBVb8r5lAkhlMg' alt='Damage seen in Dubai after reported Iranian retaliatory strikes.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Reported casualties: Authorities and newswires said four people were injured at Dubai International Airport. Separate reports said one person was killed and seven others wounded in an Iranian airstrike on Zayed International Airport in Abu Dhabi, while another report said falling debris killed a Pakistani civilian in Abu Dhabi.</li><li>Bahrain targets: Footage and reports showed strikes in Manama, including a hit on Bahrain’s National Security Agency building and another strike near a U.S. base. AP said Iranian ballistic missiles targeted a U.S. Navy facility that houses the headquarters of the U.S. Fifth Fleet.</li><li>Kuwait airport: Kuwait’s Times Kuwait said Iranian Shahed drones struck Kuwait International Airport, damaging the main terminal and causing minor injuries to several airport workers.</li><li>Spread into central Dubai: An explainer said the strikes hit areas near the Burj Khalifa as well as Palm Jumeirah, underscoring how far the attacks reached into prominent commercial and tourist districts.</li><li>Palm-area hotel fire: BBC reported smoke and flames rising from Dubai’s Fairmont The Palm hotel, as civilian areas came under fire alongside military sites.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Dubai Media Office: Dubai’s media office said an incident caused minor damage to a concourse at Dubai International Airport, and that crews quickly contained it. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/02/dubai-airport-iconic-burj-al-arab-hotel-damaged-iranian-missile-strikes'>Al-Monitor (Reuters)</a>)</li><li>Qatar authorities: Qatar said the &quot;situation secure&quot; after authorities foiled attacks, and urged the public to stay alert to rumors. (<a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/02/28/qatar-says-situation-secure-after-iranian-attacks-foiled-urges-vigilance-on-rumours'>Euronews</a>)</li><li>Bahrain Interior Ministry: Bahrain’s interior ministry urged citizens and residents to head to the nearest safe locations after strikes and drone attacks were reported in Manama. (<a href='https://apnews.com/article/iran-us-explosion-tehran-c2f11247d8a66e36929266f2c557a54c'>AP News</a>)</li><li>Euronews correspondents in Dubai: Euronews journalists said drones hit residential areas, with evacuations underway and panic in the Palm tourist district after explosions. (<a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/02/28/euronews-journalists-in-dubai-report-multiple-drone-attacks-on-residential-areas'>Euronews</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/iran-attacks-rock-dubais-palm-burj-al-arab-airport/arti